.TH FIX-HOSTFILES 1 "September 5, 2026" "fix-hostfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fix-hostfiles \- manage hosts files used by hblock
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fix-hostfiles
.RB [ \-h ]
.br
.B fix-hostfiles
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-f ]
.br
.B fix-hostfiles
.RB [ \-v ]
.BI \-a " DNS_NAME"
.br
.B fix-hostfiles
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB { prep | restore }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hblock
blocks advertising, tracking, and malware domains by mapping them to 0.0.0.0 in
.IR /etc/hosts .
.B fix-hostfiles
backs up or restores that file, adds reachable domains to hblock's allow list,
and can flush the macOS DNS cache.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command help and exit.
.TP
.B \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Display detailed paths, commands, and file metadata. For hosts-file operations,
the report includes type, symbolic and octal permissions, owner, group, size,
inode, link count, and modification time.
.TP
.B \-f ", " \-\-flush
Flush the DNS cache and restart mDNSResponder. This action is macOS-specific.
.TP
.BI \-a " DNS_NAME" ", " \-\-add " DNS_NAME"
Add a DNS name to the hblock allow list and remove its exact entry from the
hosts file.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B prep
Back up the hosts file as
.I /etc/hosts-ORIG
and run hblock to generate a new hosts file.
.TP
.B restore
Restore
.I /etc/hosts
from
.IR /etc/hosts-ORIG .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hosts
System hosts file.
.TP
.I /etc/hosts-ORIG
Backup created by the prep action.
.TP
.I /etc/hblock/allow.list
DNS names that hblock should allow.
.SH NOTES
Options add and flush are actions. They cannot be combined with one another or
with prep or restore. Run system-file operations with sufficient privileges.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo fix-hostfiles prep
sudo fix-hostfiles restore
sudo fix-hostfiles --add example.domain.com
sudo fix-hostfiles --flush
sudo fix-hostfiles --verbose prep
.fi
